# STORY: the seven villain arrival missions (claude/VILLAIN_ARRIVALS_v1.md, APPROVED John 16:39).
# Text only. BUILD wires the ids. Generated: edit story_tools/gen_villain_text.py, not this file.
extraStrings:
- type: en-US
  strings: &id001
    STR_EVENT_SS_WITNESS: A WITNESS WHO WANTS TO TALK
    STR_EVENT_SS_WITNESS_DESCRIPTION: 'SCARLETT: A Cobra bookkeeper walked into a sheriff''s office last night and asked for us by name. He says he moved the money that paid for a training camp, and he
      can tell us where.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}He also says Cobra has made a deal with someone he calls ''the clan''. He was very frightened of the clan.'
    STR_BRIEFING_SS_ARRIVAL_TITLE: 'OPERATION: SILENT NIGHT'
    STR_BRIEFING_SS_ARRIVAL: 'HAWK: Our witness is in a motel off the interstate with two deputies and a lot of coffee. We move him at dawn. Until then he''s ours to keep breathing.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Cobra
      knows where he is. Whoever they send won''t kick the door in. Expect one man, at night, and expect not to hear him.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Keep the witness away from windows. Keep your people in pairs.
      If somebody goes quiet on the radio, assume the worst and go look.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Hold until the transport arrives.'
    STR_EVENT_SS_ARRIVAL_WON: 'SCARLETT: The witness made it. He gave us the camp, and a name for the man who came for him: Storm Shadow. Ninja, Arashikage clan. Cobra''s new friend.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SNAKE
      EYES: (He reads the name and says nothing at all.)'
    STR_EVENT_SS_ARRIVAL_LOST: 'SCARLETT: We lost the witness. One arrow, through a window nobody was watching. Our people never saw him.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}We have the arrow. The fletching is Japanese, and
      very old style. Somebody in this outfit isn''t Cobra at all.'
    STR_EVENT_DREADNOKS_CONVOY: FUEL CONVOY OVERDUE
    STR_EVENT_DREADNOKS_CONVOY_DESCRIPTION: 'BREAKER: An Army fuel convoy went quiet on a swamp road in Florida two hours ago. Last call from the lead truck was ''bikers'', then music, then nothing.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SCARLETT:
      Florida State Police have it from a gas station clerk: a gang in leather, a swamp boat, and a man in a hood who paid for everything in new hundred-dollar bills.'
    STR_BRIEFING_DREADNOKS_ARRIVAL_TITLE: 'OPERATION: SWAMP RAT'
    STR_BRIEFING_DREADNOKS_ARRIVAL: 'HAWK: Somebody hired a motorcycle gang to steal ten thousand gallons of Army fuel. They''re draining the trucks into barges at a bait shop on the water.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}They''re
      loud, they''re mean, and they don''t run. Don''t let that fool you into thinking they''re stupid. The hooded one isn''t with the gang. He''s the one paying them.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Recover the trucks.
      Stop the barges. If you get a clean look at the man in the hood, take it, because I don''t think anybody ever has.'
    STR_EVENT_DREADNOKS_ARRIVAL_WON: 'SCARLETT: Fuel recovered. The gang calls itself the Dreadnoks, from Australia by way of every swamp in the South. They follow one man: Zartan. Master of disguise.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}He
      was standing next to Roadblock at the end, wearing a deputy''s uniform. Nobody noticed until he was gone.'
    STR_EVENT_DREADNOKS_ARRIVAL_LOST: 'SCARLETT: The barges got away with the fuel and the gang got away with the barges. Cobra just bought a lot of driving.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}The bikes have a name painted
      on the tanks: Dreadnoks. And the hooded man has one too. Zartan. Every report describes a different face.'
    STR_EVENT_DESTRO_ARMS_FAIR: AN ARMS FAIR
    STR_EVENT_DESTRO_ARMS_FAIR_DESCRIPTION: 'SCARLETT: Every crate with the M.A.R.S. mark has pointed one way: a castle in Scotland and the family that has sold weapons out of it for four hundred years.
      Its head is called Destro.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}He''s holding a private demonstration this week, by invitation. One of the invitations went to Cobra Commander. He accepted.'
    STR_BRIEFING_DESTRO_ARRIVAL_TITLE: 'OPERATION: TRADE FAIR'
    STR_BRIEFING_DESTRO_ARRIVAL: 'HAWK: Remember the man in the steel mask on the footage? He''s real, his name is Destro, and he''s about to shake Cobra Commander''s hand on his own firing range.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}If
      that handshake happens, Cobra stops buying M.A.R.S. weapons and starts getting them first. I''d rather it didn''t.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}His guards are professionals, not Cobra recruits. His guests are
      dictators with bodyguards of their own. Nobody here is on our side.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Break up the meeting. Grab whatever he''s demonstrating. If you can take either man, take him.'
    STR_EVENT_DESTRO_ARRIVAL_WON: 'SCARLETT: The fair''s broken up and we have the demonstrator''s prototype. The handshake still happened, in the car on the way out. Destro is Cobra''s partner now.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}But
      we cost him a buyer list and a weapon. He''ll remember that. He''s a man who keeps accounts.'
    STR_EVENT_DESTRO_ARRIVAL_LOST: 'SCARLETT: They shook hands on the range, in front of every dictator on Earth, and then they watched us leave.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}M.A.R.S. builds Cobra''s weapons from today.
      Expect better guns, more of them, sooner.'
    STR_EVENT_BARONESS_TRANSPORT: PRISONER TRANSPORT
    STR_EVENT_BARONESS_TRANSPORT_DESCRIPTION: 'SCARLETT: Washington is moving three of our Cobra prisoners to federal custody tomorrow. The route is supposed to be secret.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Someone requested
      a copy of it this morning, with clearances that check out. They check out too well.'
    STR_BRIEFING_BARONESS_ARRIVAL_TITLE: 'OPERATION: CHAIN OF CUSTODY'
    STR_BRIEFING_BARONESS_ARRIVAL: 'HAWK: Cobra knows the route. We know they know. So we''re riding with the transport.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Whoever runs this is good: real paperwork, real clearances, a real
      leak somewhere in Washington. That isn''t a field commander. That''s an intelligence officer.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Keep the prisoners in the trucks and the trucks moving. If it turns into a fight, the
      prisoners are the prize. Theirs and ours.'
    STR_EVENT_BARONESS_ARRIVAL_WON: 'SCARLETT: Prisoners delivered. The woman running the ambush got away in a helicopter: black leather, glasses, a European accent. Cobra calls her the Baroness. She runs
      Cobra Intelligence.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}She knew my name. She used it.'
    STR_EVENT_BARONESS_ARRIVAL_LOST: 'SCARLETT: They took the prisoners. The leak in Washington is real, and the woman who used it is called the Baroness. She runs Cobra Intelligence now.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Everything
      those prisoners told us, Cobra will hear about by the end of the week.'
    STR_EVENT_TWINS_BOARD: EXTENSIVE ENTERPRISES
    STR_EVENT_TWINS_BOARD_DESCRIPTION: 'SCARLETT: Extensive Enterprises has new chairmen: twins, Tomax and Xamot Paoli. Since they took over, the company''s security men have started wearing red.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}There''s
      a board meeting on the top floor of their tower on Friday. Washington has finally signed a warrant.'
    STR_BRIEFING_TWINS_ARRIVAL_TITLE: 'OPERATION: HOSTILE TAKEOVER'
    STR_BRIEFING_TWINS_ARRIVAL: 'HAWK: We have a warrant for the books of Extensive Enterprises, and a feeling the books aren''t going to be handed over politely.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}The guards are Crimson
      Guard: Cobra''s elite, men with law degrees and rifles. The twins fight together. Hurt one and the other feels it. Don''t let them stand side by side.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}There are office workers in
      that building who think they work for a shipping company. Get them out.'
    STR_EVENT_TWINS_ARRIVAL_WON: 'SCARLETT: We have the books. Extensive Enterprises was Cobra''s bank, and the twins ran it. Tomax and Xamot, commanders of the Crimson Guard.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Their lawyers
      were in court by noon. The company is ours to take apart.'
    STR_EVENT_TWINS_ARRIVAL_LOST: 'SCARLETT: The books went into a shredder on the forty-first floor while the twins went out by helicopter. Tomax and Xamot, commanders of the Crimson Guard.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Their
      lawyers were in court by noon, suing us. They''ll probably win.'
    STR_EVENT_MINDBENDER_CLINIC: THE QUIET PATIENTS
    STR_EVENT_MINDBENDER_CLINIC_DESCRIPTION: 'DOC: Six people walked out of a private clinic in Arizona this month and went home. Their families say they came back polite, calm, and somebody else.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Two
      of them have since driven trucks for a Cobra front company. Neither one remembers applying.'
    STR_BRIEFING_MINDBENDER_ARRIVAL_TITLE: 'OPERATION: SECOND OPINION'
    STR_BRIEFING_MINDBENDER_ARRIVAL: 'HAWK: The clinic belongs to a man who lost his medical licence twenty years ago. He''s back, and Cobra is paying for his research.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}The patients aren''t
      the enemy, even if they''re holding rifles. Stun them if you can. Doc wants every one of them alive.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Find the machine they''re using, and find the doctor.'
    STR_EVENT_MINDBENDER_ARRIVAL_WON: 'DOC: The patients are coming back to themselves, slowly. The machine is in our hangar. The doctor calls himself Mindbender, and he left his notes behind.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}He''ll
      build another one. But we understand this one now.'
    STR_EVENT_MINDBENDER_ARRIVAL_LOST: 'DOC: The clinic was empty by the time we were inside, patients and all. Dr. Mindbender''s machine went with them.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Somewhere tonight there are people
      who''ll do whatever Cobra asks, and they won''t know why.'
    STR_EVENT_SERPENTOR_TOMBS: GRAVE ROBBERS
    STR_EVENT_SERPENTOR_TOMBS_DESCRIPTION: 'SCARLETT: Somebody is robbing tombs. Napoleon''s. Genghis Khan''s, if anybody could find it. Every one of them a great conqueror.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}They don''t
      take the gold. They take samples.'
    STR_BRIEFING_SERPENTOR_ARRIVAL_TITLE: 'OPERATION: LAST RELIC'
    STR_BRIEFING_SERPENTOR_ARRIVAL: 'HAWK: Cobra has its list of dead conquerors almost complete. The last name on it is in a museum vault, and Cobra is going in tonight.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Mindbender is
      building something out of all those samples. Every one we keep from him is a piece he doesn''t get.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Stop the theft. Whatever comes out of that laboratory, I want it born missing something.'
    STR_EVENT_SERPENTOR_ARRIVAL_WON: 'SCARLETT: The relic stayed in the vault. It didn''t stop them. Cobra has crowned a new leader, grown in a vat: Serpentor, emperor of Cobra.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}He''s missing
      the conqueror we kept from him. Doc thinks it shows.'
    STR_EVENT_SERPENTOR_ARRIVAL_LOST: 'SCARLETT: They got the last relic. Cobra has crowned a new leader, grown in a vat from every great conqueror in history: Serpentor, emperor of Cobra.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Cobra
      Commander stood at his side at the coronation. He didn''t look happy about it.'
- type: en-GB
  strings: *id001
